-- #1111 A-2.5b SEVERITY MIRROR — a GENUINE error, with the collision present.
--
-- Its partner `method_missing_impl_no_collision` is the same genuine error with NO
-- collision anywhere.  Pinning only that one would leave the interesting half
-- untested: a fix that widens which candidates an import witnesses can turn a
-- collided graph's obligation into a MISSING one, and a missing obligation is
-- silence — a strictly worse S0 than the wrong-interface one being fixed.
--
-- EXPECTED VALUE DERIVED BY HAND: no `impl` of anything for `Blob` exists in this
-- graph, so the program is wrong under every reading.  The only question this
-- fixture grades is WHICH interface the one error names, and `msmth` reaches this
-- module only through `msmid` → `msifb`, so:
--
--   No impl of MSIB for Blob; write an 'impl MSIB Blob'.
--
-- 🚨 BEFORE A-2.5b this rejected with `No impl of MSIA for Blob` — LOUD, so not an
-- S0, but naming an interface the call never mentions and pointing the reader at
-- the wrong repair.  Same defect, S2 arm.
import msmid.{MSIB, msmth}
import msifa.{MSIA}

public export data Blob = Blob

main = println (msmth Blob)
